{"body":{"text":["A word written before 2026-11-11 also points at its lexeme, the word as one, held by one lexicon; none written since does. The lexicon is a function over the field's words now, `lexicon()`: every word said, in lower case, each once, worked out each time it is asked, as the author settled in the eighth session. Rewriting the words before it, to let their lexemes go, waits on his word, for it would add about 15 MB to the store."]},"id":"1M75ZHTCVDZK02M","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
