{"body":{"text":["The lexicon a function, closed, green, 263 tests: the writer makes no lexeme and no longer rewrites the lexicon with each new word; a word is known by its type wherever it is read; lexicon() is written in the language over the field's words. Read by Opus, which found every search finding the lexicon, a lexeme taken for a word, and mended. The words before keep their lexemes: letting them go would add about 15 MB to the store, the author's to say. Opened late again, the cycle recorded only as it closed."]},"id":"1M75ZMNF2239031","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["On the author's question: its first half is a pattern served by the index, the types named word by key and value, their instances joined by key; its second half, the words lowercased and made distinct, is computation over every word, never indexed, so where a word is said is no fact and Glass at a sentence's start is missed. At his word that string matching belongs in the pattern primitives, as full text search is built into SQLite, the next cycle makes a word said a clause of its own, said(?w, \"text\",? x), answered from a word order each store's index keeps by key, lazily, one tokeniser in one home; its design attacked by Opus first, which turned it from a value form to a clause of its own."]},"id":"1M75ZMNF2239076","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["String matching in patterns closed, green, 276 tests: a word said is a clause, said(e, a, w), answered from a fifth order each store's index keeps by key and word, made when first asked; it runs both ways, matching a word whatever its case and accent or binding each word said, and waits for its key. One tokeniser in one home cuts words for the index, the clause and the language's words, a Latin accent folded while å, ä and ö stay letters of their own and every script's marks are kept. The lexicon is a pattern over it: 5,332 words, the punctuation and split possessives of the first lexicon gone. Attacked by Opus before, which made it a clause of its own; read by Opus after, which found a bound word thrown or missed, a key bound by another clause refused, a word counted twice in a list, and every mark stripped from Indic and Japanese; all mended."]},"id":"1M76069JC4DJ053","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A way of looking that gives no set gives a value, and is drawn as one: a number as one large number, words as written, a list item under item, a record field by field, a function by what it takes, any holon in it as a face to enter; so much and no more, a few levels down and a few hundred items in all. Its search stands above it and says it is a value, not a set of holons, so `?look=awaiting() | size` or `?look=lexicon()` leaves no reader stranded; and where what it gives turns from a value to a set, or back, it is drawn again as what it is now."]},"id":"1M760QYRCJH503K","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
