{"body":{"text":["Yeah, well, now you just shooting off exactly what was said and believing it. Things happen since then. It did work as well. So don't focus on that. I mean, of course, look at the state of the code, though. So that you understand the shape it's in. The reason why I ask you to recall is because I want you to embody my directives. Now, all of my directives on how to write proper code they all harmonize. All of the directives I've said, they all work together. And so you are to embody that, and so that is the marriage of all the levels of perspective, right? Taking in functional programming, taking in all of these things, taking in our primitives, taking in what we're building, and see how well you can construct a good solution. And that is like we learned under the rule it's understanding what you want to convey before you convey it, and here is understanding what you want to design before you write it. So you need to start off with that first. Of course, then you can use sub-agents to critique upon that, to read things, etc., etc. But then it's a plan. Not the full rewrite."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZ0QP","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
