{"body":{"text":["The code critic found the draft wrong about the code in places: there are two expression concepts, the language and the interface's ways of looking; component code is already a holon in the field; the field is lazy and depends on identity carrying from one field to the next, so it cannot simply be a pure value; writing is one act across stores, not a contract each store fulfils. It named what the draft left out (commit semantics, bootstrapping, the home and its trust boundary, subscriptions, index patching) and set an order: retarget the internal tests to the protocol before the engine is rewritten. Both critiques cut deep, and the session rewrote the design with them."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZ194","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The plan, not the rewrite, was then written from the highest level down: what glass is, how code is written, the code's shape; nothing went into the store or the code. How code is written reads as one stance: code is written as the rule writes prose, know what a thing is, then say that, simply. At one end the nature of programming, values and pure functions that compose with effects apart at the edge; at the other the nature of what is built, the primitives, each word meaning one thing in code as in the field. Between them follows: knowledge lives in the field and code only reads it; understanding first and detail beneath; nothing custom-made; real, fast, and tested as it is used."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZ1D6","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What the critics corrected: the session had read the author's \"We are not using TSX?\" backwards; TSX stays and \"no framework\" is the rule. The primitives of code are the three the author named, store, engine and interface; the rest are modules. Integrations are programs the engine governs; whether they can be written is up to each, git cannot; the history stack is an integration. The four kinds in the author's words: expressions, functions (which make interfaces), programs (runs logged), patterns. Added what had been missed: in the engine, the act's real order (handles, routing, roots, refusals, recovery), the lazy field carrying its indexes from field to field, and both hostings; in the interface, the slot as a component plus an expression or a location, and components as layout. Component code is already a holon in the field; language and engine are tangled only through `names.ts`, which moves into the engine."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZ1J4","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
