{"body":{"text":["Starting now would go: give the engine's command line the ability to commit and let the author tools go, so everything after is written through the engine; make the tests the check, rewriting those that reach into the kernel and the engine's commits to go through the engine's read and commit; move what is stored using the current engine (the natives named by address, git's types, finding roots by address, each component's declaration out of its `.tsx` into its holon); rewrite each module fresh from the bottom (glass's own format, the language, the engine, then the site, with interface and components done lightly), each starting as its brief, then code, then passing tests, then one unsteered critic. The author would look in at the end of each module, not before each step. It noted the message was cut off after \"before you\" and asked whether something else was meant; otherwise it would begin with step 1."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZ2X9","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
