{"body":{"text":["The mapping of how the engine changes the field confirmed a real defect that the session's own writes that night hit: the tools mint their own ids and the engine passes an empty `born` list, so new holons are recorded as \"moved\" rather than a new run, the minter's moment guard cannot see them, and checkpoints grow (volume 24's is 148 KB against about 64 KB of lines). The store still reads correctly; the rewrite fixes it at the root by having the engine alone mint ids. It also found that an act cut short partway through its refs is never finished, and a small race between checking the head and writing it; both went into the outline."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZ350","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["With all three mappings in, the session drafted the engine design( `engine.md` in the scratchpad) on four changes: a read becomes one expression, the eleven kinds becoming functions in the language; evaluation stays pure and lazy, stopping when a holon is not loaded, the engine fetching it and evaluation running again, so one holon still costs one block; the engine alone mints ids, the act becoming six steps, route, roots, refuse, mint, judge, write, an act cut short finished on the next attach or commit, a lock covering the race between writers; about thirty built-in functions down from about fifty, the rest written in the field, with lookups such as `type` and `named` becoming patterns, measured about ten times faster."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZ38T","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The critic reading against the author's words found: the draft opened a write contract that the settled design says waits for a second writing integration; it presented reading from the first store that keeps a holon as neutral when the author had refused \"first\"; it drew indexing wholly inside the engine, against the author's words that a store may answer patterns itself; it kept `prose` as a native against the decision on the tools; several things for the author to decide went unflagged. It proposed plainer words, \"the bare language\" for \"kernel\" and \"what it lacks\" for \"needs\", and opening the engine as governance with today's faults moved out."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZ3CA","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The code-side critic was decisive in places: stopping evaluation at the first missing holon would mean about 46k passes over the wiki (14 levels, 45,906 holons), while loading every holon locally is about 45 ms; several natives planned for the field would be too slow or wrongly eager( `case`, `group`, `follow` );and the order would break the site midway without a shim. The revision was substantial, so a second, narrower round went back to the code critic on the reading, patching the field, the act's safety, the natives and the build order. It settled them with gaps closed: a read cannot know in advance which stores it touches, so it gets a bounded rerun, at most once per store, the index built lazily and the planner choosing which stores' indexes to ask; three natives were missing, `said`, a prefix clause for search, and `attachments`; stores gain an atomic replace and stale locks a rule; the new natives go into today's engine first, search fixed in the same step. A script choice was sloppy and stopped before writing anything, and was narrowed to the one brief."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZ3JA","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The engine's outline was written into the field under Glass, as designed/ The code's shape/ engine, deep enough to rewrite from. Where the first draft failed: laziness, now a read is answered either by identity, a holon or whole fetched block by block, or over stores, evaluated over whole stores loaded only when a function says it needs one, at most one rerun per store and never an answer over fewer stores than needed; the act, the cross-store write had been moved into the engine against a settled thread and stays in glass's format, the engine keeping residence, minting and judging; natives, `case`, `else`, `group` and `follow` stay built in or they would be eager or quadratic, and `said` and the prefix clause were missing; the build order would have broken search and the site midway, so now the oracle tests run green against today's engine first, the new natives go into today's engine, and the old forms of read are translated until every published store has caught up."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZ3QR","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
