{"body":{"text":["No, we don't need to churn so much before. I mean, we can go ahead and then do all kinds of, you can show me how you think that you're gonna do and prove to me that you're embodying different principles, etc. But it's not necessary, I think. Go ahead, do a rewrite, make sure to cycle enough. Cycles are important, and with cycles, there is a certain amount of exploration, open-mindedness that is needed. Have the ability, of course, to embody different kind of perspectives and reviews, such as different schools of thought, principles, what would Rich Hickey say, what would, I mean, and so on, right? Uh, Comparing with OpenLight, all kinds of, I mean, bringing in fresh energy all the time, um, and just do that rewrite and do it to the best of your ability, and then simply I will look at it, and if I think, hey, we can orchestrate things better, or hey, did you perhaps you should think about this and that in regards to these principles, I'll say so."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZ5EY","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The session took it as no more preparation: the rewrite now, in cycles, each reviewed from fresh angles, the author looking at the result. It goes on its own branch, `engine-rewrite`, so `main` stays whole; built in layers bottom up, the oracle green, each layer reviewed from several perspectives (Rich Hickey on simple against easy, values and what is complected; functional and Unix; the rule's gradient; a comparison with OpenLight's engine; the author's directives) and revised before the next. During the move the new engine carries the old natives the field's functions still call, in one file marked to go, so the repository keeps working."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZ5JC","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Layer 1a was built: moulds in one home, judging as small named rules, the act as ordered pure steps, the engine minting every id, with the fix for ids landing as \"moved\" and every writer moved to handles. `engine.ts` reads as a table of contents, down from 411 lines to 125; 312 tests pass, typecheck clean; committed on the branch as d4656e2. A reviewer on Fable read it from five angles: Hickey, functional and Unix, the gradient, OpenLight's engine (cloned from the author's public repository), and a skeptic of the design itself."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZ5NC","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Most of the review held, finding real defects: judging is quadratic, a regression of about 12 s at 32,000 holons; a hole at the root, where a change including its store's root leaves loose new holons held by nothing; `{ \"$ref\": \"garbage\" }` commits silently; `actOf` is not the clean read-then-pure seam its header claims. From OpenLight it brought a dry run collecting every problem, so a change can be judged without writing it. The builder revised 1a from the six must-fixes, three improvements and the naming and ordering changes, and it was committed. Layer 1b was then being built: writes replacing a file rather than overwriting in place, exclusive locks recognising stale ones, the browser's home held across tabs, an act cut short finished or its stores refusing writes until it can be, to go through the same review cycle."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZ5SV","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
