{"body":{"text":["To check the register it drew today's read path: `answer(field, expression)` chooses between two paths; `evaluator(world)` is a closure memoised per world, keeping what it learns; `evaluate(expression, scope)` recurses over forms, a scope a chain of closures' words; `natives(calling)` is handed `apply` and `evaluate` back and invokes them in return, as `map` does, the invocation that in return invokes; `world.log(key)` throws a Lack that `answer` catches before reading the log and evaluating again, control returning by exception. At this register it showed that evaluator and natives are mutually recursive through closures handed both ways, and that the Lack is a hidden second channel up the stack. If that is the register, next would be the whole engine drawn so, as it is, then as settled this session, then held up to the schools."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZHJH","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
