{"body":{"text":["`evaluator(world)`, in `engine/read/evaluate.ts`, makes the bare language for one world and returns `evaluate(expression)`, `apply(fn, values)` and `truly`, a re-exported helper nothing should take from there. Made once per world and kept in a WeakMap, it finds the function types (every holon named \"function\" with a mould: a lookup by name, not by address, which the settled direction forbids), builds `calling` (its own apply and evaluate plus the world), calls `natives(calling)` for three tables of closures (given: `get`, `map`, `eq`; lazy: `if`, `case`, `and`; structural: `find` ),and keeps a mutable `depth` counter shared by every read of that world against runaway nesting."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZHPE","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The world, in `engine/read/world.ts`, made by `worldOf` on the first `field.world()`, is every attached store read whole into memory and joined: `stores`; `known` (id to store, holon, block; the first store wins); `byStore`; `place` (the field's order); `holders(id)`, the reverse of every reference built by scanning every body; `storesOf(id)`; `mouldFor`; `index()`, built when a pattern first asks and kept on the `shelf` for the next field; `log(key)`, which throws a Lack if the history is unread. For this repository: about 140,000 holons loaded in about 330 ms, then reverse references and residence in about 170 ms, before any expression is evaluated."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZHST","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["So `evaluator` is not really a function of an expression but a closure factory over a whole-field snapshot, the world being the field reified as one big in-memory value. That is why a one-holon read on a cold field cost about a second, and why evaluator and field are coupled through `world` rather than a narrow interface: the natives reach straight into `known`, `holders` and `index`."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZHW1","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
