{"body":{"text":["Not sure I like the packing of a world like that. It gives me the unit feeling again. I think the engine should be able to be really naked. Now you take you handle something and take it through what it has to be taken through. I think maybe it's kind of a bit object-oriented anyway consider. How simply and powerfully we've broken down things today. For me to go through the engine offers to look at each offer and understand it, to go in a simple journey as I read through the code. And again, as we're not building unit, we're looking at what happens from beginning to end in offers. We think about how we make most artfully and simply draw that using the components we create. They're honoring the nature of how we do things, of course. Components have various levels in the realm if it be it to things can be done so very differently. I'm still waiting for the right presentation"]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZJG2","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The engine drawn naked: no world, no field object with methods, no units holding things. The engine is a handful of offers, each a journey: something comes in (an expression, a change, a store) and is taken through its steps until it comes out a value, an act, or problems. The components are those steps, named by what they do. It keeps plain data: at hand (holons read, what refers to each, where each resides, the index's facts), in flight (changes under way with their reach), followed (reads followed and what each read). Everything else is a function of these."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZJKD","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The journeys: `read`: expression → resolve names against what is at hand → evaluate (patterns asked of the index, holons not at hand fetched from their stores) → value. `follow(expression, told)`: a read kept with what it read, read again and told when what it read is touched and the value changed. `commit`: reach (what it writes, lets go, refers to, is an instance of, from its bodies alone) → order (waits only for changes in flight it meets) → place → mint ids for handles → judge (rules, over what is at hand and what was ordered before) → write (an act per store: blocks, line) → offer to each head, which accepts or says it moved → take in → act; refused at any step → all its problems. `heard(store, acts)`: read what they wrote and let go → take in, the index patched by those holons alone → answer every followed read touched. `mount`: follow the head, what it holds becomes reachable; `unmount`: stop following, take out, answer again. Five offers and one thing heard; a commit here and a move elsewhere both end at take in."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZJSG","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Components by level: offers (the top and nothing else); steps (resolve, evaluate, reach, order, place, mint, judge, write, offer, take in, answer), each a function used wherever needed, take in and answer serving three journeys; parts beneath (natives, the index's facts and solving, rules and moulds, blocks and line); outside (stores, storage, buffers), reached only by mount, offer and read."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZJVE","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
