{"body":{"text":["The author was right about stores and the session had drawn it wrong: every arrow in `interface > engine < store < buffer < runtime` is one relation, one side subscribing and able to ask or offer, the other telling. So the engine subscribes to each store it mounts, and the store tells it of every act it accepts, from this engine or another. Offering is separate, its reply only accepted or refused and why. The engine takes in its own commit when the subscription tells it, as anyone else's: one path for changes, not two. `heard()` was a store's `told`; as an offer it was a confusion; it is simply `store.subscribe(takeIn)`."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZK82","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
