{"body":{"text":["`atHand`: the engine's data of what it has read (holons by id, what refers to each, residence, the index's facts), a value every step reads and only `takeIn` replaces. `inFlight`: changes under way with their reach, read by `order`. `takeIn(act)`: called by a store's subscription; puts the act into `atHand` (new versions in, what went out, references updated, the index patched by those holons alone), then answers every subscription the act touched. Taking an act in twice is a no-op since acts are known by content, so commit reply and store telling may arrive in either order."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZKCB","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Two kinds of going wrong, not sharing a path. Refusal is expected: problems as a value, all at once, never thrown, at only two places: judge, and offer when a store refuses because its head moved. Failure is unexpected (storage unreachable, a block failing its hash, a code fault): thrown, caught only at the edge of an offer and stated to whoever asked; one read's failure never reaches another's; a subscriber is told it as its read's current state and told again on recovery, as Serving already does."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZKF7","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Handles: if mint comes after judge, problems speak the caller's words(\" `~2` refers to something that isn't there\") rather than unseen ids. Today it is place, mint, then judge; the session would flip it. After minting the act carries which handle became which id. So `commit`: `reach`; `await order(reached, inFlight)`; `placed = place(change, atHand)`; `problems = judge(placed, atHand)`, returning `{ refused: problems }` if any; `act = write(mint(placed))`; `answer = await offer(act, mounts)`, and if moved, `return commit(change)` (what moved was taken in by subscription and is judged again); else `{ act, born: act.born }`. Refusal travels as a value out of judge and commit; failure as a throw to the offer's edge."]},"id":"1M78WEQVZBZZKJE","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
