{"body":{"text":["I don't know if that's to be first class thing, because really we know that if an integration is responsible for projecting its field, but it also allows for consumers to, shall we say, post to that field, then of course you could just create that phenomena. It could be the one list for the committed output, another list for where you place your input. The thing about it is that it's in cycles. So of course, really, all of this could be orchestrated on top. It needn't be a first-class thing, exactly. We know that sources have the ability to define the type in which they exist. But again, Git goes both ways. What if you want to commit? What if you want to edit something? Is that then a program? Is that it? I don't think so. You wanna allow direct edits. So then a source that is alive like that isn't a one-way thing. So then a unit of integration is not inseparable. It's not separably input or output. Do you understand the kind of perspective I'm taking?"]},"id":"1M7J7W9674MT0Y8","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
