{"body":{"text":["Well, okay, so then what is your proposal for the primitives? How do you chart the ontological lay? Even though I don't have the bandwidth, I can still talk about what makes sense and not. And considering Git, for instance, one thing is to read. Well, an integration towards Git is a program that needs to run continuously, sometimes maybe, possibly not. Possibly if the integration is only towards Git on your system, then you could use Git hooks or something like that. In the case of Git, you'd want to segregate through sovereignty and wholeness here your store and Git. So you'll be able to reference a file, then you're referencing into the store of Git, so to say. But in order to serve that, it is not saved in the format as the strata is. So you might then be able to run a program that takes, right, the remote endpoint takes HTTPS for a repository and then spawns it completely as a virtualized structure, right? And if you want to do edits, you could do that as well. There's many nuances there. And another one is that maybe you just want to project a fake repository. Can you do that? Like, you just want to emanate something. But yeah, down to the core, down to the wire and what's needed of the wire. Yes, it's true, I haven't pulled everything together for me. I haven't settled everything. But it's not to say you can't progress and evolve this topic."]},"id":"1M7J7W9674MT21J","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
