{"body":{"text":["You're following things blindly. That is absolutely not your role. Identity is made through the field and referenced like a holon. Why? Sometimes that's the truth. I can spawn a buffer because I want to use it for a string. But if I connect my audio interface, am I going to spawn a channel then? Or are the channels already there? The point was that a buffer's information is external, but a buffer such as a string could still be matched against. But I'm not sure that you are understanding that here. That's a buffer contains its parts, but may be resolved to a type within a strata-based store, right? That whilst I'm typing in my search bar, that string does not have commits for each entrance, and it lives in a separate integration, for the lack of a unified language now, and I may then reference that buffer and it may still be typed matched to the argument of something. But when it does, it becomes an in-place primitive value of a string, for instance. That phenomenon is something that perhaps has to be first class, right? So that means that we are prescribing a certain available mechanic. Now, is that tied to something that we are defining as a buffer exactly? I do not know. I'm looking upon everything that we're looking at here, that interfaces, and considering what is what's here. Perhaps we have another structure moving forward, and if we don't set the right structure, we're going to have to understand it later anyway. And then we're building the completely wrong thing, maybe. So it's a vital turning point to orient ourselves around this."]},"id":"1M7J7W9674MT31T","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
