{"body":{"text":["The session ran eight more panelists from systems that solved computing's basics (logic, combinators, lenses, content-addressed code, reactive, rewriting, actors, types). They agreed that finding is decided once and written into the use, ambiguity shown as a standing state like `#REF!`, as OpenLight's 'the mount records the pick'; that the way back is a put, `put(new value, old source)`, offered as a commit and judged, ambiguous puts refused, with the laws GetPut and PutGet and stable printing; and that faces are never chosen silently: held is the default and a value is asked for by type. Types rejected the session's candidate breakthrough, a brief collapsed or full being zoom, not type; reactive added a third face, the change. They split on whether direction belongs to the primitive: logic and constraints for an undirected relation, rewriting, combinators and actors against a separate use at all. New was that a link must say when it points (pinned, live, previous), the content-addressed voice flagging Knowledge's rule that code names by address as the weakest binding, and that a derived answer is a commit recording what it read, as settled at 16/60. Traps: action at a distance, dependencies the engine cannot see, plumbing becoming the program."]},"id":"1M7R4Z0KHV0D6ZT","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["So is there already, or rather say, which are the top contenders across all of cultural and scientific history for compute that are doing what we are doing?"]},"id":"1M7R4Z0KHV0D70S","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The session said no one has built the whole, and set out the closest, each to a different part: Xanadu, NLS, Smalltalk through Glamorous Toolkit, Mathematica, Eve, Dynamicland, TiddlyWiki, Genera and CLIM, federated wiki and Solid, Datomic and Unison, with an older lineage from Llull and Leibniz through Otlet, Bush and Luhmann to Pāṇini, Koestler, Whitehead and Alexander. They stalled for four repeating reasons: a silo, never shipping, no history, no sovereignty. Glass's claim is the combination none made: holon identity with full history, sovereign stores that meet, one primitive for knowledge, code and interface, and matching by shared nominal types; the danger lies in shipping something small and not becoming a silo."]},"id":"1M7R4Z0KHV0D74F","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["So perhaps I'm thinking if we study a bit here, there ought to be people who understood this but never fully made it to the degree that we are. Right? You name Kostler, for instance. If we consider the fullness of history, there's of course various failures, but who's to say that those authors embodied the full understanding? And there ought to be pieces and people, philosophical, such as Kostler and others, who see it from their perspective. And then there ought to be, if we look upon everything here, there ought to be also other things that contain parts of it. I mean, I'm thinking about all kinds of things, functional programming world, all kinds of things. So let's proceed more."]},"id":"1M7R4Z0KHV0D78K","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The session ran eight panelists on the thinkers who saw part of it. Five fields came independently to direction being a reading (Bateson, Chomsky, Pask, Ranganathan, Peirce), so the weight leaned toward an undirected primitive with direction supplied by whoever reads it, mathematics dissenting; Pask's meshes suggested 'under the rule' is itself a reading, a head chosen in a mesh. On when a link points, Whitehead, Frege and Nelson gave links into the settled past, pinned the default, and Maturana and Varela and Martin-Löf asked for a stated rule of what keeps a holon the same across commits. Matching is an act and should be a holon of its own. Glass has built the self-assertive side of stores but not the integrative (Koestler's Janus, Ostrom's governance between stores, Margulis's merging, Grothendieck's sheaves). It warned that holding is not referring (Leśniewski), that everything kept need not be shown, that nominal types make finding by authority, and of the literacy test (diSessa, Papert), and named one underrated person per field, among them Tarde, Ranganathan, Pask, Rosen and Jonathan Edwards."]},"id":"1M7R4Z0KHV0D7EC","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Sounds to me like there's very split schools here. I don't know precisely of what the contenders that you've raised, because I do not know them and because it would take more for me to get to know them. I can't quite say their value. Rich Hickey for me is cleared. But maybe it's stupid to clear someone as an absolute pure source of opinion. If we look upon our primitives and what we're doing, I don't get it. It's so promising what we're doing. Yet it could have been written without AI long ago. It gives me a feeling like most people are consumers of something and then they evolve things that they consume. It's cool how wide you've gone for sure. And it sounds like perhaps each person has something to contribute. Oh, I found your table now. The underrated one from each field. I don't know. I don't know how much this diving has really helped us here. Ultimately, we're talking about a kind of link, but to me, the link is unidirectional, right? Or it allows for things that are unidirectional. Because if something parses it, it must be able to place it back. It's like a codex. It's a babel fish in a way. No, it's not. That's one directional. But that is something we're exploring now, definitely. And we know what expressions are. So it's just you're able to express expressions like this in the field. How does it relate with holding? Because holding is namespacing, and that's also what makes you not have to hit 10 hold-ons at once flat in an unstructured way just because an expression takes 10 hold-ons. Expressions so far are able to be visualized as nodes, but when we connect both ways like this, I don't know, to me it's really interesting. It's the quantum link. It's a particle, that's linked in two places. It's interesting."]},"id":"1M7R4Z0KHV0D7SB","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The session conceded the deep dive bought less than its length: it confirmed the open questions and split where the author is split, deciding nothing. It found the author's instinct close to Rich Hickey's identity as a succession of values, which answers when a link points: pinned is a value, live is the identity. It agreed a link has one direction and goes both ways only through a codec obeying the laws, which reconciles the schools, and read the quantum image as one thing in two places under two spellings. Holding is the namespace, a tree and never circular; referring crosses anywhere; so a two-way link is always a reference with a codec, never a hold, and an expression's node graph is a whole and its held parts. It offered to write the codec link down against the location example."]},"id":"1M7R4Z0KHV0D7XY","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
